LRC(14) OPEN-Q-108  THREAD C: the EXACT meaning of 56 (opus2)

==============================================================================
READING 1 -- C(8,3)=56 : the 56 three-subsets of the k=8 offset set {0..7}
==============================================================================
  3-subsets of {0..7}: 56 total (= 56 = A000568(6))
  classified by support-3 relation status:
    ('AP',): 10
    ('AP', 'Schur'): 2
    ('Schur',): 7
    ('none',): 37

  This is a labeling of the 56 triples by {none,AP,Schur,both}. It is a
  4-COLORING of C(8,3), NOT a tournament.  56=56 here is the trivial identity
  C(8,3)=A000568(6) -- a numerical coincidence, no orientation structure.
  # AP triples in {0..7} = 12; # Schur triples = 9

==============================================================================
READING 3 -- the 56 triangles of K_8 (project core: 3-cycles of a tournament)
==============================================================================
  K_8 has C(8,3) = 56 triangles.  A tournament on 8 vertices assigns
  each triangle a type (cyclic 3-cycle / transitive).  The OCF counts 3-cycles.

  consec {0..7}: 19 of the 56 triangles carry a support-3 relation
    (the 'active' cells of the relation code = the binding challengers).
      ('AP',): 10
      ('AP', 'Schur'): 2
      ('Schur',): 7
      ('none',): 37

  KEY DISTINCTION: the 56 here is the # of CELLS (triangles), the SAME 56
  for ANY 8-coordinate offset set.  The DATA that varies with E is WHICH
  cells are active (carry a relation) -- analogous to which triangles of a
  tournament are 3-cycles.  A000568(6)=56 is a RED HERRING; the structural
  56 is C(8,3) = # triangles of the k=8 relation code (independent of E).

==============================================================================
DECISIVE -- active-triangle patterns of k=8 offset sets (up to S_8 relabel)
==============================================================================
For each 8-set E in a window, form the set of active triangles (those with a
