  8-sets in [0,10]: 137 distinct active-triangle patterns
  8-sets in [0,12]: 510 distinct active-triangle patterns
  8-sets in [0,14]: 1144 distinct active-triangle patterns

VERDICT printed in main().

==============================================================================
VERDICT
==============================================================================
56 = C(8,3) = # triangles (support-3 cells) of the k=8 relation code Lambda(E),
which numerically equals A000568(6)=56.  This is a COINCIDENCE of C(8,3)=56=
A000568(6), NOT a structural bijection: support-3 challengers are 3-UNIFORM
(unoriented) hypergraph cells, while tournaments are ORIENTED graphs; the
abstract support-3 shape count (358..2537) and active-pattern count are not 56.
The project-native reading: the 56 cells = the 56 triangles of K_8, the EXACT
analogue of a tournament's 56 triangles -- THIS is the real tournament link
(triangle = potential 3-cycle), but it is C(8,3), not A000568.

DONE.
